A||||6||ezsurf||Transmission Seal||||5||
Z||000000||ezsurf||11-20-2000||08:00 PM||||I've got an 86 SE 4 spd manual, and it looks like the transmission seal on the drivers side where the axle joins the transmission is leaking.  I hate to ask, but can please give me an estimate of the amount of work invloved to replace it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||11-20-2000||08:10 PM||||<BR>I have an article on my website<P>go to <A HREF="http://www.thefieroclub.com/members/~fieromag/" TARGET=_blank>www.thefieroclub.com/members/~fieromag/</A> <P>click Sections, choose "In the Garage" and you will find the article.<P>Hope it helps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-20-2000||08:41 PM||||quick summary<P>Remove the spindle nut from the CV shaft. (This is much easer with the wheel on. Use the spare if Aluminum wheels don't cooperate.) take off the wheel once the nut is off.<P>Separate the ball joint by removing the bolt at the bottom of the casting.<P>pull out the axle. A little awkward but it will come out.<P>CAREFULLY pry out the seal. If you scar up the tranny case the new seal will leak unless you fill the scars with sealer. Don't use any more sealer than required or you'll get boggers in the tranny. not so big a deal with a stick but not good either.<P>The whole thing only takes and hour or 2 max. You need a 30mm socket for the spindle nut.<P>NOTE if you hear a click noise from the axle after this repair, and it wasn't there before, then you likely don't have the nut tight enough.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||01-07-2001||12:48 PM||||ahhh I cant load up the weblink!<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||01-07-2001||06:34 PM||||If you do this your self don't just 'pull' on the axel. Find a long screw driver or narrow ended pry bar to pop the end of the axel from the trans. If you pull on it to remove, you can pull the CV joint apart!||||reg||1
Z||000005||opm2000||01-07-2001||06:58 PM||||I think your supposed to use a special tool to protect the new seal when you stick the axel back into it.   If you like, I have a whole bag of these "special tools", you have to buy 50 at a time.   Send me your mailing address & I'll send you one.<P>David Breeze<BR>N777H<BR>||||reg||1
